# Keep the build context to sources.
#
# This is not only about size. `COPY ui/ ./` would otherwise copy the
# developer's node_modules over the result of `npm ci`, replacing a clean
# lockfile-exact tree with whatever happens to be on the host, and hand Next a
# local .next cache from a different checkout.
ui/node_modules/
ui/.next/
ui/out/

# The built UI must come from the UI stage and nowhere else.
#
# `make ui` leaves a build here, and `COPY . .` in the Go stage would copy it
# in — so an image built on a developer's machine embeds whatever they last
# built rather than the current source, and one built in CI (where the
# directory holds only a placeholder) does not. That is a difference between
# environments that produces a UI missing a page nobody can reproduce locally,
# which is precisely what it did.
pkg/api/ui/*
!pkg/api/ui/.gitkeep

.git/
.dev/
bin/
dist/
*.tfstate
